# Next bounded task after C260 contract delivery

First reconcile the saved C260 handoff, its live scope and actual published
main. Confirm that the contract was independently reviewed, required checks
passed, its branch was merged and final archive/restore/save succeeded. Do not
treat package-freeze pending fields as proof that a later operation failed.

Implement **one finite read-only hinge-declaration observer** under
[CONTRACT.md](CONTRACT.md), version 0.1.0. Keep its source-derived facts,
untrusted GLB claims, comparison and historical byte admission separate. Cover
the literal signed-basis axes, literal angular limits/initial values, ordered
site associations and explicitly source-only site compatibility. Preserve
missing artifact provenance and unsupported-expression refusals.

Use the exact read-only dependency/input bindings. Independent review must
derive values separately and execute [CONTROL-PLAN.md](CONTROL-PLAN.md), with
source-only, artifact-only and paired supported changes. A fixed baseline
answer table or a producer sidecar cannot implement the observer.

Do not expand into site-pose evaluation, combined pose-authority validation,
general expression support, complete C255 semantics, a runner, source rebuilds,
native/model trials or new assets. If implementation is too large, select a
coherent smaller interface boundary and preserve the remaining obligations
without claiming whole-component completion.

Use one branch for the active scope, preserve recoverable evidence, integrate
after its applicable review/checks, verify branch deletion or ask for cleanup,
then create and verify one saved handoff and stop. Preserve all previous
failures, historical source hashes and the explicit C234 cleanup disposition.
